      "answer": "The customer whose issue started after the 2026-02-20 taxonomy rollout is BlueHarbor Logistics. Their problem was that Event Nexus search relevance degraded, with saved searches returning poor and duplicate results, increasing manual triage time to about 6 hours per day. The proposed proof plan to get them comfortable with renewal involved a short-term fix: updating index weighting and adding a mapping layer to translate new taxonomy terms to old query terms for the top 20 saved searches. This proof would run as an A/B test in staging for 7-10 business days, aiming to achieve a top-5 correct hit rate of at least 80% for prioritized queries, with no regression in suppression logic and acceptable latency. The plan included a 90-day professional services engagement at $48k fixed price, with a 30% discount if BlueHarbor committed to expanding Orchestrator seats concurrently, and a conditional credit on renewal if the proof failed to meet the agreed metrics. This approach was designed to demonstrate measurable improvement quickly and reduce manual triage, addressing BlueHarbor's executive mandate. [art_8b0063fbb3cb, art_0bccc580184e, art_bd3560dfe194, art_c9970c1dc932]",
