      "answer": "Among the North America West Event Nexus accounts, the following customers are dealing with taxonomy/search semantics problems:\n\n- Arcadia Cloudworks: search relevance degradation after taxonomy v2.1 rollout causing missing or low-ranked results and playbook trigger misses (~28%) [art_90991e25335f].\n- BlueHarbor Logistics: search relevance degraded after taxonomy rollout on 2026-02-20, with saved searches returning poor and duplicate results, suspected schema registry version mismatch [art_8b0063fbb3cb].\n- CedarWind Renewables: search relevance for incident lookups fell significantly after taxonomy update, with noisy results and legacy weights still applied [art_10f7e8b72e09].\n- HelioFab Systems: search relevance dropped after March 2026 taxonomy refactor, with missed dedupe matches and irrelevant results affecting runbook triggers [art_9345d5653840].\n- Pacific Health Network: low-relevance matches and misfiring runbook triggers after taxonomy update on 2026-03-02 [art_4eccfd9dcf29].\n- Pioneer Freight Solutions: low-relevance matches and manual triage increase due to schema version mismatch between Event Nexus index and Asset Management service [art_3ba29fe1e026].\n\nThe only account explicitly noted with duplicate-action problems (role provisioning lag and duplicative accounts) is related to WorkforceOne events after February 2026 org restructure, involving 'scim:role_map_missing' and 'approval:pending_manual' errors, affecting Learning Ops and Corporate HR [art_d11447325b44].\n\nTherefore, among the North America West Event Nexus accounts, the majority are experiencing taxonomy/search semantics problems, while the duplicate-action problem is specifically reported for WorkforceOne-related accounts in Learning Ops and Corporate HR. No other North America West Event Nexus accounts are reported as primarily dealing with duplicate-action problems. [art_90991e25335f, art_8b0063fbb3cb, art_10f7e8b72e09, art_9345d5653840, art_4eccfd9dcf29, art_3ba29fe1e026, art_d11447325b44]",
